{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_umt5vms4rnnezu3uek46bute7brd4jujtgit6cd3ppjknfj3sqbq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases passed, and I found and fixed one real bug.\n\n## The library\n\n`c_src` is a single function — `float half2float(uint16_t h)` — a table-driven half-to-float converter backed by three `static` tables (`m__mantissa[2048]`, `m__offset[64]`, `m__exponent[64]`).\n\n## Phase A artifacts (in `translation/`)\n\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — C `.so` exports exactly 1 symbol (`half2float`); Rust exports it too. Diff empty. The three tables are `static` in C, so they must *not* be exported — verified they aren't.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — mechanical grep for `if`/`switch`/`assert`/`return NULL`/error enums/range checks found **zero matches**. The function is total: `n = h>>10` is always 0–63, and `(h & 0x3ff) + m__offset[n]` is always ≤ 2047. So the table has **no rows**; I documented why and instead covered 6 generic boundary classes (B1–B6).\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — no runtime flags and no features exist, so I derived the axes from the *data-driven* branching: I read the literal contents of `m__offset`/`m__exponent` to find the 6 regions the code actually distinguishes (note `m__offset[32]` drops back to `0x0000`), crossed with mantissa boundaries → **27 rows**.\n\n## The bug I found (Phase C, row B5)\n\nC's prologue **narrows the argument register to 16 bits** (`mov %edi,%eax; mov %ax,slot; movzwl slot,%eax`). Rust marks `u16` params `zeroext`, so LLVM assumed the caller pre-extended and emitted a **32-bit** `shr $0xa,%edi`, then **elided the `m__offset` bounds check entirely**. A caller that mis-declares the prototype as taking `uint32_t` (ABI-identical on x86-64) caused an out-of-bounds read of `m__offset` followed by an index-out-of-bounds panic — an `abort`, since this crate uses `panic = \"abort\"` — where C returns a normal value.\n\nWorth flagging: my first fix, masking with `& 0x3f` inside the function, **did not work** — I checked the disassembly and LLVM had deleted the mask, because the `zeroext` assumption is precisely what proves it redundant. Masking can never fix this. The working fix declares the exported parameter at full register width (`c_uint`) so LLVM loses the assumption, then narrows explicitly with `as u16`, reproducing GCC's prologue; the faithful `u16` signature is kept via `#[cfg]` on non-x86-64. The exhaustive test confirms this changed nothing for any valid input.\n\n## Verification\n\n- 37 tests, all loading **both** `.so`s via `libloading` — the Rust is never called directly, so the `#[no_mangle]` wrapper is under test.\n- Comparisons use `f32::to_bits`, never `==`, so `+0.0` vs `-0.0` and NaN payloads are actually distinguished (`==` would have hidden both).\n- **Row 26 is exhaustive over all 65,536 inputs** — since the domain is only 16 bits wide, this is a complete proof of equivalence, not a sample.\n- `verify.sh` runs the matrix: 3 feature combos × 2 profiles = 6 configurations, all green.\n\nTwo false-confidence traps I caught in my own work, worth noting since both would have produced a bogus \"pass\":\n1. My first negative-control run silently never applied its mutation (a failed `cp` short-circuited the chain), so the tests were passing on unmutated code. After fixing it, a single altered table entry failed 14 tests including the exhaustive sweep — the harness has teeth.\n2. `verify.sh`'s symbol-parity check wrote to `/tmp`, which is read-only here, so it compared two empty files and printed **PASS**. It now uses `$TMPDIR` and refuses to report parity unless it can actually see `half2float` in the C `.so`.\n\nI also verified all three tables element-by-element against the C source (2048 + 64 + 64 values, all equal), `cargo check --all-targets` is warning-free, and `c_src/` is unmodified apart from the `build/` directory the instructions told me to create."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1262,"cache_read_input_tokens":89204,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1262,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"feb4f6a7-2251-4a5d-8622-b2985cdc3866","uuid":"052295eb-9c2f-4656-87b8-cbb57f614057","timestamp":"2026-08-26T21:59:35.343Z"}
